from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path('docs/mechanical/fusion-controller')
mesh=json.loads((R/'mesh-check.json').read_text());sl=json.loads((R/'slice-report.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'));t=json.loads((R/'final-targeted-checks.json').read_text());service=json.loads((R/'service-path.json').read_text())
assert len(mesh)==len(sl)==27 and all(r['Success'] for r in sl) and not t['clashes'] and not service['clashes']
for n in [3,5,7]:
 q=json.loads((R/f'motion-{n}.json').read_text());assert len(q['poses'])==53 and not q['clashes']
closure='''\n## Implementation closure (same review round)\n\nThe reviewed findings were implemented in scripts19,20 and22. Final crossblock rows are Y=-70/-62 at Z53.5, with the block extended toY=-74 (1mm inside the rail); this supersedes the intermediate -62/-54 proposal, which crossed a cup guide. Installed-insert outer wall is at least1.7mm for an assumed4.6mm OD, with ample cam-side wall. The guide bores remain separate. Rotor clamp with flat washer pad, default4.2mm and optional4.1mm coupling grooves, M5x30/5mm-total metal rail spacers, 2mm preload collar, M3x35 guides and M4 socket head are present.\n\nFinal neutral CAD check finds only0.000634mm³ numerical cam-contact overlap. The three cam profiles each passed53 sampled poses. After corrections,27 additional rotor/coupling poses, operating/service follower positions, +/-1mm preload movement and optional tight-disc assembly fit passed the0.01mm³ threshold. Revised cam withdrawal at5mm increments through40mm with the follower depressed5deg passes. Exported cam profiles track the intended roller center within0.0013mm over the159 sampled positions (mesh/facet approximation). These checks do not replace physical force or fatigue tests.\n\nAll27 final print meshes are single connected, closed, consistently wound solids, bed-oriented and inside the256mm P2S envelope. All27 final slices succeeded;12 use conventional supports. The largest part is171mm long. Vendor CLI preset/tool-command warnings are retained in logs; only geometry is released, not that G-code. Guide/BOM explicitly retain actual RK097, T-nut engagement, spring choice, free-sliding coupling and reversal-hysteresis checks. No additional review round was commissioned.\n'''
for name in ['FINAL_FDM_REVIEW.md','FINAL_MECHANICAL_REVIEW.md']:
 p=R/name;s=p.read_text();s += closure;p.write_text(s)
report='''# Fusion controller validation and release evidence\n\nThe exact original 640 x190 x110mm frame was retained as grounded mesh reference. Native printed components and hardware envelopes are separately named. Three revolute joints and two rigid groups assist inspection; they do not solve spring/contact dynamics.\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Neutral assembly | No unintended overlap above0.01mm³; intended cam/roller numerical contact0.000634mm³ | neutral-validation.json |\n| 3/5/7 cam travel | 53 poses each over +/-52deg, no overlap above0.01mm³ against components and conservative frame envelopes | motion-3/5/7.json |\n| Revised rotor/coupling and spring fixtures | 27 rotor poses, follower operating/service positions, +/-1mm preload, tight-disc neutral fit: pass | final-targeted-checks.json |\n| Cam service | Depressed follower, sideways cam extraction0..40mm in5mm steps: pass | service-path.json |\n| Profile/roller contact |159 poses, maximum absolute gap/penetration below0.0013mm | cam-contact-check.json |\n| Printing meshes |27 single connected manifold meshes, correct winding, bed atZ0, P2S fit | mesh-check.json |\n| Slicing |27 successful layer generations,12 with normal supports | slice-report.json |\n| Expert review |One final FDM and one final mechanical review; findings implemented and targeted checks completed | FINAL_FDM_REVIEW.md; FINAL_MECHANICAL_REVIEW.md |\n\nThe insert relocation, rotor clamp, reduced coupling clearance, rail spacer stack and spring-loaded service procedure are the principal review-driven changes. The guide contains the print and assembly sequence and complete hardware list.\n\nThe geometry package deliberately excludes generated G-code. Bambu Studio CLI2.4.0.70 reported preset metadata/nozzle-volume and invalid-tool-command diagnostics despite generating layers successfully. Re-slice supplied oriented STLs using the user's installed P2S printer profile; inspect supports before printing.\n\nPhysical fit, sensor range, coupling reversal play, T-nut engagement, spring force/solid height and fatigue life are prototype checks. RK097 dimensions remain assumptions until measured; the mount and shaft clamps are replaceable.\n'''
(R/'VALIDATION.md').write_text(report)
print('Final geometry/slice evidence and review closure recorded')
